{"schema":"semaprax.canonical-loan-source-before.v1","base":"8086b7e5047e7199c8fccb2f07c49c3513982d2a","rows":[{"path":"docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","after_length":394768,"after_sha256":"20fdbcf1ec5fefc07b95342fea78b1e30edcd3ebf22a052b196cb0a9a0db0a41","before":"# Compiler architecture\n\nStatus: living internal implementation and trust-boundary map.\n\nAudience: compiler contributors and reviewers.\n\nUse this page to find the code that owns a behavior and to see where trust\nchecks happen. It is a contributor map, not a feature catalogue. For other\nquestions, start here:\n\n- current status: [completion matrix](COMPLETION-MATRIX.md);\n- exact protocols and ABIs: their versioned reference documents;\n- required checks: [quality gates](QUALITY-GATES.md);\n- history: [changelog](https://github.com/wavect/semaprax/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md).\n\nThe key rule is separation: readable source, checked meaning, agent reports,\nwrite authority, and target execution are different things. Passing data\nbetween them does not automatically transfer authority.\n\nThe test-only `source_reflows::front_pool` module owns the bounded edit-string pool\ndecoder shared by the source-front readers. Its Python counterpart lives in\n`test_v12_view_labels.py`. They reconstruct existing source DATA without adding\nsource or archive authority; [the source contract](SOURCE-CUSTODY-OVERLAY-V2.md#source-front-edit-string-pool-v1)\nowns the exact wire-derived expansion bound and opaque metadata rules.\n\nFor a first read, follow [System shape](#system-shape),\n[Representations](#representations), and\n[Trust boundaries](#trust-boundaries-and-invariants). If you are changing code,\njump to the [repository map](#repository-map),\n[module-size rule](#module-size), or\n[integration-test harnesses](#integration-test-harnesses). The detailed owner\nnotes below are for locating an implementation, not a prerequisite for writing\nyour first program.\n\n`src/workflow_profile.rs` and its `enabled` submodule own the optional\n[current-thread workflow observer](WORKFLOW-PROFILING-V1.md). Instrumentation\nis absent without its Cargo feature; observations never enter canonical\nproducts or acquire authority. `benches/workflow_observer.rs` and the performance\ncampaign runner own measurement, exact product comparisons, and host metadata.\n\n`benchmarks/cross-language-v1/supported_scope.py` owns the read-only comparison\nsupport projection. It reuses v3's no-follow source snapshot and fixed correction\nadmission, retains every task/adapter slot, and adds support/exclusion metadata.\nIt has no toolchain dispatch or scoring path and does not change v1/v2/v3\nexecution authority. [Runnable adapter v3](CROSS-LANGUAGE-RUNNABLE-ADAPTER-V3.md)\nowns the actual official TypeScript admission and runtime evidence.\n\n`benchmarks/cross-language-v1/agent/pilot_{protocol,run,score}.py` and\n`claude_subscription.py` own the additive [live laboratory pilot](CROSS-LANGUAGE-LIVE-PILOT-V1.md).\nThe protocol binds all inventory rows; transport owns explicit subscription\nand bounded process authority; the candidate session reuses independent v3\nDarwin admission with a disjoint candidate overlay. It does not widen the\nfixed-source v3 route. `agent/pilot_linux_host.py` and\n`agent/pilot_linux_launcher.c` separately own the [Linux VM scoring profile](CROSS-LANGUAGE-PILOT-LINUX-HOST-V1.md):\nexplicit image/toolchain pins, Landlock/seccomp confinement, physical denial\nprobes and reuse of the same candidate/assertion bridge. The controller remains\nDarwin; native guest model generation is a separate transport grant. Receipt\naccounting grants no execution or independent-review authority.\n`agent/pilot_linux_provider.py` and `agent/pilot_linux_runtime.py` own\n[provider guest provisioning](CROSS-LANGUAGE-PILOT-LINUX-PROVIDER-V1.md): signed\nnative CLI admission, private interactive login, pinned isolated CPython and\ncredential-free committed source projection. They grant no model-dispatch\nauthority; the frozen native transport remains the sole dispatch route.\n\n`benchmarks/cross-language-v1/agent/specialization_accounting.py` owns the\nread-only [specialization cell accounting](../benchmarks/cross-language-v1/agent/README.md#issue-326-frozen-cell-accounting-blocked).\nIt authenticates retained original protocol/task metadata and selected current\nsource bytes with the existing bounded no-follow reader, then invokes the\nunchanged specialization v1 plan builder. It neither imports a provider nor\nreads task trees, executes an oracle, accepts approval or emits model results.\nThe original 81 cells and nine later additions remain distinct. Nonzero blocked\nstatus and missing independent-review/custody records cannot confer authority.\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/skeleton_work.rs` ordinary construction uses the explicit-payer renewal, moving-string, condition and lexical-owner collectors. It prepares the held ReplayBudget refusal/census backing before any collector allocation; original collectors and the complete previous constructor remain independent test controls. No allocation-funding claim is inferred from a transfer optimization.\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/skeleton_work/merge_search.rs` owns the source-only retained\nmerge search candidate shared by borrowed path/call grouping and owned suffix\nrows. It stores only local search scalars, eliminates callback/compound-result\ntransport and pays every surviving dynamic index/comparison payload. Complete\nimmediate and earlier producers remain independently compiled; no runtime gain\nis established by this module map. See [the contract](RETAINED-MERGE-SEARCH-OWNER-V1.md).\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/ordinary_plan_history.rs` and its children own the private\nordinary ActiveBuilder PLAN history candidate. Immutable segments use backward\narena indices; child paths retain a segment index and a short owned tail.\n`producer.rs` builds the complete plan set, and prepaid forward cursors compare\nits observations and terminals with the unchanged flat HIR multiset. Its\nfallible heapsort orders comparison-owned paths only. Canonical runtime cleanup\nvectors retain their original order. `before.rs` independently compiles the\ncomplete flat predecessor. Selected, Oracle, renewal and lexical/factored\nreplay remain outside this route. `source_reflows_merge/ordinary_plan_inputs.rs`\nowns its bounded, sealed historical source acquisition. This ownership map does\nnot establish runtime qualification or application savings; see the\n[candidate evidence](evidence/ordinary-plan-history-c8740045-v1/README.md).\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/skeleton_work/enumerated_prefix` owns the private ordinary\nnonmerging HIR sequence-storage candidate and full-content cursor comparison.\nIts dedicated Seq/Cat constructor uses ordinary free work and the existing\nprepaid iterative destruction frontier. Both flat and immutable PLAN comparison\nroutes consume full HIR observation content; marker/pointer identity carries no\nsemantic authority. Existing path state and runtime cleanup order stay intact.\n[The source contract](ORDINARY-ENUMERATED-HIR-PREFIX-V1.md) records pending\nexecutable/physical/application qualification and the unchanged resource limits.\n\n## System shape\n\n```text\ncanonical .spx source or held Project inputs\n                    |\n              lexer + parser\n                    |\n                 AST\n                    |\n        resolver + semantic verifier\n                    |\n          validated stable-ID HIR\n                    |\n       canonical cleanup-plan builder\n                    |\n          independent plan replay\n             /       |       \\\n semantic graph   interpreter   target lowering\n      |                         /            \\\n context/impact/review      native C11    Wasm Core\n      |                          |             |\n evidence + transactions      Clang       JS/Node host\n```\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/path_array/sequence_minimum/optimized` owns the shipping\npaid no-growth header at the original lexical first-output work frontier. It\npays before every new selected/iterator/arithmetic receiver, then declines a\nproved unchanged capacity or pays the complete old query envelope. The useful\ncapacity predicate covers both paid frames. The complete immediate receiver,\nold minimum helper, original tests and Main44 controls remain independent.\n\nEvery backend passes source verification and validated HIR. Cleanup-plan vectors\nare canonical runtime order; projections and backends must never sort or repair them.\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/paid_type_facts/inventory_summary` owns the ordinary schema\ncaller's streaming inventory validation and retained summary. Its lifecycle,\nshape and expression children preserve complete validation before publication;\n`schema/paid_summary` selects it only with the existing builder-like ReplayBudget.\n`cleanup/schema_summary` owns the ordinary compatibility receiver: the complete\nordinary validation walk retains summary flags and one last slot instead of\ndiscarded inventory directories, without a replay budget or physical payer. Its\nfirst profile failure is selected after the complete traversal, as before.\nComplete original inventory and test-only schema materializer remain independent\nexecutable parity controls. Other schema probes retain their existing owners.\n`cleanup_plan/replay/expression_facts/receiving/directory/status_prefix` owns\nordinary status insertion and optional immutable membership lookup storage.\nIts active builder holds paid mutable search scratch only during insertion;\neach subsequent row resets it and performs the complete original comparison and updates.\nAfter every current row and producer passes validation, an active-builder\nreceiver retains its paid bit index alongside the complete AVL keys. Each query\nauthenticates the exact function, replay budget, invocation and immutable key\nbacking before reading the index, then decides membership by full-key ordering.\nPublication seals mutation; rejected owners stay rejected. Other payers retain\nthe original lookup. The index grants no verification or source authority.\n`hir/canonical_loan_storage/caller/shared` owns immutable lookup publication\ninside the existing captured preparation owner. Active compatibility validators\nand nested closures share exact-program storage; unobserved compatibility owns\nexplicit unobserved inventory custody. Original receivers remain independent.\n`hir/validation/stdin_stream/paid` owns the active constructor's borrowed streaming\npreflight and complete paid derivation. The original receiver remains separate.\n`hir/function_directory/caller::prepare_shared` prepays immutable compatibility\nlookup custody; nested validators retain the same exact-program directory and\nrepeat the original checks. Inline scratch is not a language limit, and other\nconstructor preflight allocations remain separate unproved owners.\n`byte_data_capacity/witnesses.rs` owns optional bounded transcript-refusal help\nreconstructed from the same checked flow after the primary refusal is selected.\nIt pays cursor, spill, visits and output through the existing invocation ledger;\ninsufficient optional capacity omits help without replacing a sticky refusal.\nThe hidden `reserve_transcript_witness_preserving` library facade exposes only\nthat reservation operation to the independently compiled model harness. It\ncreates no ledger, quota, credit or authority. Compiler-only witness controls\nare registered in the library harness; the original standalone model controls\ncontinue to compile against their complete receiver and the real payer bridge.\n\n`cleanup_plan/renewal_history.rs` owns private path-local staged-epoch tracking\nfor authenticated owned-element Vec renewal. Builder and replay derive their\nown transfer mappings and exact atomic call commits; staging never debits the\nreserved history. This tracking retains no declaration index and changes no\nserialized proof authority or physical cleanup operation.\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/lexical_replay/ordinary.rs` owns the paid ordinary lexical\ncaller. Its fallible return-operand index in\n`expression_facts/receiving/return_operands.rs` borrows exact HIR identities and\nuses the existing paid AVL directory. The index binds the held function, lexical\nfacts, ReplayBudget and current ledger, authenticating before exit membership\nand certificate replay. It carries no certificate or source admission authority.\nSelected/no-owner callers retain their preceding route; the full old ordinary\ncaller is retained as a complete independent test module in `lexical_replay/before_operands.rs`.\nThis is a source-only checkpoint with owning execution pending.\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/factored/strategy.rs` owns deferred lexical resource selection\nand post-authentication Enumerated/LexicalFactored dispatch. Exact certificate and\nownership replay precede observation-automaton construction; terminal census alone\nhas no authority. Expression-scoped Copy discovery closes before caller-prefix\nsequencing. The held automata, weighted proof and selected physical backing share\none cumulative ledger; the selected provider/type profile remains separate.\nFitting ordinary lexical replay retains the complete Enumerated admission\npreflight and held upper, then consumes that same Candidate's weighted proof\nwithout a second HIR/plan enumeration. Canonical work uses ordinary free work;\nheld enumeration units are not refunded or lent. The complete immediate-old\nentry stays independently compiled in `strategy/before_fitting.rs`, and explicit\ntest forcing retains the old enumerator and its real over-limit refusals.\n\n`hir/expr_nodes.rs` keeps complete Result/Option residual types in the funded\n`ResolvedResidualType` box, reducing the common expression layout. Resolution\nand generic materialization acquire the new backing and receiving controls\nbefore construction. Retention censuses include each box; the authored pre-bound\nconservatively includes its backing too. The private cache codec delegates to\nthe original Type codec without adding a wire tag, node or depth level. A\ncomplete previous expression module remains compiled as the layout, full-field,\nDebug and clone-backing control, and both source inventories inspect it.\n\n`cleanup_plan/replay/compact_stage.rs` owns the private staged-result observation\nrepresentation: body fields stay inline and residuals retain the complete\ncanonical source behind prepaid backing. Canonical CleanupPlan data remains\nthe admission and replay input. Its test children retain the full original flat\nplan producer, observation shape, header traits, and lexical marker producer;\nthe live producer and borrowed-key comparator retain all semantic work.\n\n`factored/paired.rs` owns the ordinary positive synchronous weighted-language\ncomparison after the existing automaton and lexical admission boundaries. Its\nfunction/budget/current-ledger bound invocation acquires actual scratch and\nprimitive receiving frames; complete owning return carriers remain per-call.\nIt compares complete labels and checked multiplicities by value, retaining the\npreceding canonical comparator for every inconclusive result. The proof grants\nno source, publication or physical cleanup authority. [Paired weighted\ncomparison v1](PAIRED-WEIGHTED-COMPARISON-V1.md) owns its qualification boundary.\n\n`factored/canonical_shared.rs` owns ordinary immutable weighted payload sharing\nfor both ordinary and selected lexical canonicalization. Moved vectors retain\nfull backing reservations; Rc headers, frame slots and map nodes acquire their\nactual layouts before construction. Sharing keeps the original len-plus-one\ncopy work and zero-byte sticky payer authentication. The complete original\nreceiver remains in test-only `factored/canonical_before.rs`; source-custody\ninverses join its full interior and the HIR authority scan includes both owners\nand their receiving controls. `canonical_shared/ordered_alias.rs` owns the exact\nnon-sink/no-moves/single-epsilon immutable closure receiver; it retains every\noriginal route/skeleton work request and authenticates the same held memo owner.\nThe complete a33 receiver and BTree alias helper remain test-only controls in\n`canonical_shared/before_alias.rs` and `canonical_shared/epsilon_alias.rs`.\nQualification and application fit remain pending.\n\n`canonical_shared/ordered_weights.rs` owns the numeric closure/closed-accumulator\nAVL arena, with paid dense node backing and parent-linked ascending iteration.\nNumeric keys never index directory capacity. Published closures are immutable;\na unit-singleton closed state borrows its authenticated closure, while general\nweighted states retain a separate paid arena. The original weighted traversal,\nchecked arithmetic and exposed work requests remain unchanged. State/signature\ndictionaries keep their preceding trees. Persistent singleton successor states\nuse `canonical_shared/inline_weighted.rs`: One and Many keys compare their exact\nordered contents. One keeps its paid tuple inline in the shared allocation;\nmoved roots and general successors retain their fully paid Vec backing. Enum\nreceivers and the actual shared layout are acquired before construction. The\ncomplete immediate receiver is `before_inline_weighted.rs`; qualification and\nany physical benefit remain pending.\nThe complete immediate BTree receiver is retained in `before_ordered.rs`; full\nsource inverses and allocation-free comparison adapters preserve older controls.\nThis source-only draft's focused qualification is pending.\n\n`canonical_shared/paid_many.rs` owns the composed ephemeral label targets:\nfirst/repeated One stays inline; a paid distinct-child promotion uses the\nexisting fallible flat-vector physical owner, bounded search and sorted shifts.\nThe unobserved route retains tree Many. Both actual successor families acquire\nnew helper/return/iterator layouts before formation; sorted output retains the\nsame immutable sharing, arenas, compact nodes and cold Memo. No budget ceiling\nchanges. Selected replay uses the owned outer label tree with inline One targets. The\nGroups label transport is retained only as an independently compiled immediate\ncontrol: its additional receiving banks exceeded the removed tree cost in the\nobserved singleton case. Distinct children still use the paid flat producer;\nempty and repeated-single-child routes retain the exact preceding tree producer.\n`before_selected_route.rs` retains the whole immediate canonical receiver and\nall its original Groups banks. This repair is source-only; renewed qualification\nand physical comparisons remain pending.\n`successor_targets.rs` remains the complete old One/tree-Many type for\nindependent controls. `before_paid_many.rs` and its terminal/comparison children\nretain the complete immediate receiver and actual production comparison caller;\nall old helpers/tests remain source-bound and all children join the three raw\ninventories. Focused executable and application qualification remain pending.\n\nThe source-only #884 candidate keeps the actual ordinary canonical frame loop\nin `canonical_shared/lexical_successors/frame_loop.rs`. Its two lexical\nsuccessor expansions retain separate primitive caller banks per activation;\nfresh label/target/iterator/owning payloads remain paid per formation. The\ncomplete immediate receiver and production comparison caller stay compiled in\n`before_lexical_successors.rs` and its child. Fixed diagnostic counters and\nfocused controls do not grant authority or establish gain. See\n[Lexical canonical successors v1](LEXICAL-CANONICAL-SUCCESSORS-V1.md); combined\nsource binding and runtime qualification remain pending.\n\n`hir/resolve_program/initial_loan_plans.rs` owns the initial authored and\ninstantiated loan-plan attachment. Active construction captures one existing\nCFG reservation and funds complete planner scratch. One caller-held staging\ndirectory stores groups of at most 32 plans inline (roughly 20 KiB of bounded\nstack storage); larger groups acquire an exact paid heap directory after the\nfirst complete plan. The same directory is cleared between authored and\ninstantiated groups.\nEach group installs only after its complete collection succeeds, with authored\nattachment preceding instance planning. The later canonical caller still\nrebuilds and compares every full plan independently; initial attachments grant\nno admission or sizing authority. Unobserved construction keeps the legacy\nplanner. Linked-workspace metadata rebuilding uses the same current-member\nattachment boundary. Linked byte-slice provenance borrows authored functions then\ninstances through the unchanged full derivation instead of cloning their HIR.\nDeclaration-index disposal sends only nominal children to its existing iterative\nfrontier, so scalar leaves and empty nominal arguments need no queue.\n`loan_plan/funded_flat.rs` owns the exact-current-member paid planner,\nwhile `bounded_output/cfg_reservation.rs` owns its affine ledger and prepaid\nphysical-refusal carrier. `loan_plan/cfg_directory.rs` owns private mutable AVL\nscratch for paid CFG identity, root, point and edge directories and endpoint\nlive sets. Private candidate/planner alias, binding, ownership, parent and\nnonconsuming inventories use the same paid directories; `directory_access.rs`\nkeeps borrowed receiver dispatch separate from the saved BTree policy, and\n`origin/funded.rs` retains the original projection constructor with a paid\nborrowed-reference cycle set. `paid_live.rs` owns private seed/live/edge receivers;\nthe paid draft parameter leaves the public BTree draft unchanged. Predicate and\ntraversal active/allowed sets share those nodes. Borrowed cursors prepay two\nreferences and use O(n log n) successor traversal; consuming drain remains linear.\nSticky removal moves existing nodes without allocation or refund. Missing nodes are prepaid before mutation; unique rotations and\nordered extraction allocate no additional nodes. The public BTree planner and\ncomplete saved planner retain their independent storage policies.\n\n`hir/validation/identity_directory.rs` owns the validator's private ordered\nexpression/value identity sets. Its sealed keys share immutable backing.\n`transaction.rs` borrows the current root while paying and constructing a\nshared or weak suffix, then mutates the unique prefix and rotates without\nfurther fallible work. Each actual new Rc node acquires its owning carrier and\nliteral initializer before construction. Snapshots share a root; duplicate\npriority precedes acquisition. `iter.rs` provides allocation-free ordered\ncursors with an address-space bound derived from private AVL construction.\n`identity_insert.rs` preserves caller order. The complete saved function,\niterative, recursive and closure receivers use independent original BTree\nstorage through test-only entry adapters; the original conservative BTree\nreceiver and full controls remain in `identity_insert/coarse.rs`. Whole-chain\nand directory controls retain exact/short sticky refusals, complete identity\nstate and actual allocation through Drop. Requested allocation and cumulative\nacquisition remain separate: shared path copies may allocate more than an\namortized BTree insertion. Qualification and application recovery are pending.\n\n`hir/closure/paid.rs` and `paid/copy.rs` own the private validation product's\ncanonical identity/result backing and literal parameter/body constructors.\n`hir/validation/closure.rs` routes all four direct identity insertion sites\nthrough the existing constructor payer, retaining capture and merge diagnostic\npriority. The copied root is a direct `ResolvedExpr`; child boxes retain their\nactual constructors. Shared declaration/value/expression identities clone without\nnew backing. Complete shape validation and the three ordinary canonical plan\nbuilders retain their order and work, and remain residual funding domains.\nRecursive scalar and fixed affine/mutable/borrowed admission defines the copied\nvariant/statement inventory; a complete legacy fallback preserves future profile\nbehavior while explicitly remaining unpaid. Metadata types beyond the existing\nbounded replay clone census likewise retain a complete unpaid clone rather than\nintroducing a shape refusal. The original public product and full\nsaved receiver/corpus stay independent; source-only controls make no allocation\nor application recovery claim.\n\n`hir/validation/scope_checkpoint.rs` owns private persistent ordered ownership\nscopes. `hir/validation/function_scope.rs` seeds parameter bindings directly\ninto that paid scope, validates the body through the existing checkpoint-target\npublication guard, inserts the full provisional result, and lends persistent\ninputs to independent contract baselines. Parameter/result type payload clones\nand tree insertion backing are prepaid before construction. A sealed paid owner\nholds the mutable scope borrow through the one consuming insertion; dropping it\nbefore insertion preserves the prior root. The complete prior\nmap function is retained in `function_scope/old.rs` beside the saved expression\nand contract drivers; all children are joined into the validator source audit.\n`hir/ordinary_scan.rs` owns private inline preflight scratch and paid spill backing.\n`iterator_loop/paid.rs`, `iterator_loop/renewal/paid_scan.rs` and\n`validation/unsafe_scan/paid.rs` retain distinct traversal and error order;\nrenewal streams borrowed children without a per-node temporary vector. The\nfunction scope adopts these variants at the existing preflight positions and\npropagates boolean scan refusals as errors. Full original scan bodies and the\noriginal renewal owner remain compiled test receivers. Physical qualification\nand application acceptance are pending; no quota or budget cap changes.\n`hir/declared_collection/paid.rs` owns the current function's borrowed collection\npreflight, and its `early.rs` child owns the unchanged early profile traversal.\nTyped pending and ordered-set backing is paid before construction; an existing\nborrowed invariant lookup replaces discarded formatted identities. The complete\noriginal collection receivers remain in `declared_collection.rs`.\n`function_scope/lifecycle/completed.rs` owns one function's monotone required-effect\nset and completed exact zero-argument lifecycle roots. Successful roots borrow\nidentities from the immutable program; generic instances retain the complete\nfunded collection route. Inline keys select storage only, with prepaid spill\nbacking and sticky authentication on every hit. The complete prior function\nreceiver remains compiled in `function_scope/lifecycle_receiver_saved.rs`.\n`function_scope/lifecycle.rs` owns borrowed declared-effect keys, borrowed active\nlifecycle identities and prepaid distinct imported effect payloads. The complete\noriginal lifecycle collector remains in `inspection.rs`; the complete prior\npaid function receiver also remains in `function_scope/backing_saved.rs`. These private owners\npreserve the original structural bounds, traversal and diagnostic order; combined\nfocused physical qualification remains pending.\n\n`hir/owned_text_record/paid.rs` owns funded executable text containment and\ntext-record admission, with the existing paid collection shape receiver retaining\nthe complete fallback. Owned substitutions retain their independent semantic\nroute and pay each actual backing constructor. The complete prior executable\nreceivers remain in the owning `saved.rs` children.\n`hir/validation/executable_profiles.rs` owns one exact immutable-index observation\ndirectory shared by primary validator clones and nested closure validators.\nOnly known zero-argument non-generic record observations are memoized; every\nrequest authenticates sticky refusal, and per-expression validation remains\nindependent. The reference-counted carrier and directory backing are prepaid.\nPhysical qualification and complete validator funding remain separate.\n\nThe map-entry adapter retains map publication and its charges. Persistent inputs\nhave no physical publication map; their guard returns the selected root on Drop.\n`scope_checkpoint/transaction.rs` pays each actual node carrier and owning Node\ninitializer while staging an immutable shared suffix. A scalar depth identifies\nthe unique prefix; the sealed scope borrow pins it until infallible publication\nand rotations by unique Rc access. Binding carriers precede owned payload clones;\ncopy insertion shares existing binding and identity handles. Sticky zero-byte\nchecks also cover allocation-free replacement. The full former `3 * height + 8`\nreceiver and tree insertion remain independent controls in `coarse.rs`/`tree.rs`.\nNo allocation or application-fit improvement is claimed before qualification.\nBranch, loop, match and source-move checkpoints share immutable roots;\nmutation pays for copied paths and full binding payloads before copying. Output\npublication moves the last complete state into prepaid map slots after child\ncheckpoints drop. Nested guard publication restores a private scope directly. Contract validation\nuses `scope_checkpoint/fresh.rs` to inspect every current flag and share clear\nbindings/subtrees, paying complete true-flag payload clones and changed node\nconstructors before returning a staged baseline. Empty/clear baselines retain\nsticky refusal. Its immutable root is shared across independent clause mutation\nand publication domains; the full-copy baseline/tree builder remain test oracles.\n`hir/validation/record_pattern.rs` retains complete record-pattern admission\nagainst the same ordered read/write interface. Neither owner accepts attached\nproof authority or changes the validation traversal or admitted language profile.\n`hir/validation/generic_template/values.rs` owns the separately paid persistent\nordered symbolic directory: keys retain existing identity handles and types\nborrow the exact immutable current HIR. Wholly unique insertion paths prepay\nthe leaf before mutation; shared paths publish only a complete paid replacement.\nContract, block, branch, match, loop and closure environments preserve their old\nisolation boundaries. Complete old borrowed-map and owned-map test receivers\nremain independent. [Validator Scope Checkpoints v1](VALIDATOR-SCOPE-CHECKPOINTS-V1.md)\nowns private storage/payment invariants and remaining qualification obligations.\n\n`hir/validation/byte_range.rs` re-derives named-slice and exact inline\nowned-Bytes range origins from live scope. Source loan origin bookkeeping\nindependently retains the same owner for immutable composed-range locals;\ncall admission and both HIR walkers consume that borrowed authority without a\nnew retained declaration index or carrier schema.\n\n`hir/validation/call_parameters.rs` owns validation-only byte-operation\nsignature views and argument ownership checks. Byte views borrow the immutable\noperation table and format synthetic parameter identities only for diagnostics;\nother signatures retain their owned metadata and full frame capacity census.\nThe test-only recursive validator retains the allocating signature reference.\n\n`string_ops/take.rs` owns the exact named-String transfer shape. Source and\nindependent HIR admission retain availability/loan authority; cleanup producer\nand replay derive operand moves separately. Engines forward the same canonical\nargument/result carrier, with no new runtime identity or public ABI.\n\n`literal_format.rs` owns the closed decoded-template scanner and reserved\noperation identity. Source verification and HIR validation independently\nadmit its dedicated `ResolvedExprKind::LiteralFormat`; the cleanup planner\nstages dynamic owned arguments in ordinary CallArgument epochs. The native\nand Wasm emitters use private rendering workers, while Project snapshot replay\nre-resolves format-bearing synthetic source before accepting retained HIR.\n\nThe private retained record carrier is produced by\n`workspace_graph/static_text/record_closure.rs` before defining HIR is filtered.\n`source_schema/static_text/primitive/helpers/types.rs` authenticates demanded\nflat declarations against that source revision and namespace, then exposes the\nactual borrowed type members through `ReplayContext::type_count/type_at`.\n`primitive/records/prepared.rs` compares layouts and constructs the minimal index\non the same preparation ledger; imported type names and layout facts alone grant\nno helper-body or owned-construction permission. The borrowed-record scalar\nproducer and independent replay receiver restrict reads to current borrowed\nparameter roots and exact declared scalar fields.\n\nThe additive retained scalar import route captures defining-source facts in\n`workspace_graph/static_text/scalar_helpers.rs` before HIR filtering. Its\n`scalar_helpers/capture_directory.rs` child precharges borrowed lookup and\nauthored-order selection storage, classifying each eligible body once; source,\nsignature and digest authentication still precede inventory publication.\n`source_schema/static_text/primitive/helpers.rs` authenticates the demanded acyclic\nclosure and exposes exact borrowed function members across modules; imported names\nnever enter the consumer's local declaration-name index. Its `helpers/graph.rs`\nchild walks each selected body once against a balanced borrowed directory holding\nonly the caller's functions and already selected external members in publication\norder. Charged comparisons, growth and rotations preserve that order; reached\nmembers reserve storage on demand. The closure retains the directory for later\nlookup, records contiguous outgoing-edge ranges, and visits each edge once in\nKahn order; a directory hit carries no authority, so first discovery still\nruns unchanged target authentication and its provider receipt. The private\n`cleanup_plan/replay/selected_entry.rs` preparation transfers its single work and\nbacking ledger into the existing session, while `scalar_replay.rs` independently\nreplays each nonlexical scalar helper. `hir/borrowed_scalar.rs` checks exact Borrow\nStr/Slice parameter roots and supported scalar read/conversion call shapes;\nits Option-u8 child holds independent canonical metadata predicates, with\nproduction Option receiving admission kept closed pending cumulative lookup and\nschema metering. The unchanged lexical driver replays the\nconsumer. Broader imported nominal/loan/intrinsic profiles remain closed and #745\nremains open; authored execution and allocator controls await qualification.\n\nProject execution selects interpreter closure admission from the retained manifest\nprofile in `interpreter/resolved_case.rs`. Project v25 stream-text and its v27\nstream-data successor admit pure, explicit-ID owned-String helpers with the\nchecked parameter/result shapes. V27 additionally admits shared\n`Vec<Copy scalar>` parameters only on authenticated non-root helpers.\nEntry, ordinary/named tests, cancellable execution and prepared-origin closure\nmaps use that same selector. Legacy interpreter and Project profiles retain\ntheir existing closed maps; this selection grants no host effects or authority.\n\n`hir/copy_record_collection.rs` and the independent source classifier own the\nbounded flat Copy-record Vec element shape. `hir/collection_outcome.rs` and\n`source_verify/declared_type/collection_outcome.rs` independently classify direct\ntwo-case results with one or two of these owned vectors; ordinary variant\nlayout and conditional cleanup own transport, without new graph authority.\nThe independent `collection_outcome/stream_input` classifiers compose exact\nnormalization owners with these existing results; [the join contract](INPUT-COLLECTION-OUTCOME-JOIN-V1.md) preserves ordinary carriers and settlement.\nNative lowering lives under\n`native_emit/expression/vec_ops/copy_record.rs`; Core Wasm lowers the same\nchecked field words in `wasm/aggregate/vec_copy_record.rs`. Both retain one\ncanonical Vec owner and the existing scalar storage ceiling. Project/profile\nadmission remains an independent boundary. The explicitly selected Project v29\nstream-data successor uses `hir/workspace_link/stream_record.rs` to authenticate\nits retained nominal closure and exact codec outcome shapes after the existing\nowned-data linker reconstructs source-owned declarations. Native and prepared\ninterpreter routes recheck that selected profile; v27 remains frozen.\n`hir/declared_collection.rs` and its source twin separately own logical text\ncollection declarations with no runtime carrier authority. Both reject every\ntransitive executable use, including uncalled functions; [Declared Text\nCollections v1](DECLARED-TEXT-COLLECTIONS-V1.md) owns that explicit boundary.\n\n`source_verify/declaration/record_shape` owns the ordinary owned-Bytes record\nshape diagnostic and exact six-field diagnostic dependency used by error-only\nrecovery. Real parameter bindings retain their original type and ownership;\nonly a dependent match shape is unavailable after the same declaration refusal.\nIndependent body expressions, parameter modes, lexical pattern checks and valid\nrecord patterns continue through their existing owners.\n\n`ast/type_properties.rs` owns primitive type formatting and classification.\nThe reserved mutable callable type has independent source and retained-HIR\nadmission guards in `source_verify/declared_type.rs`, `source_verify/closure.rs`\nand `hir/validation/callable_types.rs`. Leaf type helpers remain under their\nexisting graph, Wasm, capacity and workspace owners; `properties/scalar_types.rs`\nowns the property analyzer's scalar spelling projection.\n\nThe staged transactional carrier is owned by `hir/closure/mutable.rs` (fixed\nstate/argument body product and independent receiver checks),\n`interpreter/mutable_closure.rs` (copied state and scoped invocation guard),\n`codegen/native_emit/mutable.rs` (success-only native publication), and\n`wasm/aggregate/function_value.rs` (guarded indirect call and state commit).\nThe Rust interop builder's `public_sdk/mutable_callback` renderer retains the\nactual source-created native carrier behind an exclusive safe Rust owner.\nThese internal products do not remove the source or HIR admission guards.\n\n### Agent and generic owners\n\nThe additive `agent_lifecycle/iterative` module owns checked Step transitions,\nper-turn authorization, bounded stage execution, and iterative evidence. Its\nstep validator maps checked variant fields back to exact State/Result records;\nthe frozen one-pass lifecycle retains its existing owner. The `iterative/effects`\nmodule binds scalar operation registries to deployed contracts, meters calls and\nencoded argument/result bytes, and validates host results before reduction.\n`agent_runtime_v2` exposes the direct consuming producer implemented by\n`execution_revision/typed`; it owns exact invocation inputs and joins evidence\nonly from the run it actually executes. The private `iterative/driver` reserves\nstages and exposes the effect and transition boundaries to\n`iterative/effects/durable`, which owns the trusted-store execution adapter.\n`agent_runtime_v2/checkpoint` owns only the closed journal codec and accounting;\nits hashes confer no authority. The durable producer replays checked stages and\nfresh authorizations before accepting retained host observations, charges replay\nfuel, and stops on uncertain delivery. `execution_revision`\njoins retained Project source, ProgramRoot, deployment, invocation and actual\nlifecycle evidence through opaque consuming producers. These associations grant\nno host authority. The generic collection helper under `hir/generic_collection`\nowns exact private Box/Vec signature admission; source verification and HIR\nmaterialization independently validate concrete substitutions.\n\nThe additive durable target selector in `iterative/effects/durable` and the\njoined Runtime v2/migration wrappers forward only caller-held native compiler\nor Core Wasm runtime capabilities into that same journal driver. The target\ndoes not enter checkpoint identity or grant effect authority. A linked Project\nwithout exact retained Wasm source refuses selection before the initial\nmigration handoff store commit; accepted replay still checks the ordinary\nidentity, limits, grant and observation sequence before further dispatch.\n\nPrivate generic collection and iterator-helper admission lives in\n`src/source_verify/declared_type/generic_collection.rs` and the independent\n`src/hir/generic_collection.rs` profile. Existing monomorphization and HIR\nvalidation check all eight concrete Copy substitutions; Box/Vec interpreters\nand backends consume the same canonical cleanup plans and runtime carriers.\nThe [owning specification](GENERIC-COMPILER-COLLECTIONS-V1.md) defines the exact\nprivate signature boundary.\nThe [generic iterator profile](GENERIC-ITERATORS-V1.md) reuses those source/HIR\nclassifiers for scoped `Iter<T>` and `IterStep<T>`, with exact Step field\nidentities and independent match-binding ownership validation.\n\nAuthored generic variant admission is owned by the independent\n`source_verify/declared_type/generic_variant` and `hir/generic_variant` profiles.\nThe HIR validator checks all concrete substitutions and match bindings.\n`cleanup_plan/build/generic_variant` produces the canonical arm-result and\ncontinuation transfers; native and Wasm helpers consume those transfers in\norder. Private workspace signature admission checks retained declaration facts\nin both workspace collection and HIR linking. Public signatures retain their\nseparate admission boundary.\n\n## Representations\n\nThe registry compiler and unpublished toolchain share one compiler library and\n`src/cli_driver.rs`. The root dispatches; `context_dispatch.rs` owns the\nbounded source, Project, and prepared Rust API context routes;\n`options.rs` parses bounded command options, `report_options.rs` parses report/analysis options, and\n`source_execution.rs` owns single-file build, run, and diagnostics.\n`diagnostic/writer.rs` borrows caller output for shared JSON/human rendering; the CLI report path owns its stream lock. Active bounded JSON retains the complete legacy renderer and its logical quote order. Neither writer nor stream lock certifies prepaid report/output storage.\n`help_dispatch.rs` prints the global and scoped `cli::help` surfaces.\n`cli/help/authoring/tasks.rs` owns V6 fixed task/profile pages over an embedded scaffold-derived descriptor and the existing library catalog. Its test child rederives complete manifest/source/import bindings; help itself performs no host I/O or source compilation. The old V5 cards and v2-v8 scaffold capsules retain their owners and bytes.\nThe `source_execution.rs` module’s `fused_profile` child dispatches the explicit source-only profile before\nordinary checking. Public `fused_source` parses once and lends a private full\nselected owner to each target; it accepts no caller HIR or grant.\n[Fused source profile v1](FUSED-SOURCE-PROFILE-V1.md) owns the finite caller\naccount policy and pending executable admission qualification.\n`cli_driver/native_test.rs` owns explicit bounded execution of Project v26/v28\nnative test artifacts; `project/native_test.rs` selects only authenticated test\nroots and reuses the existing native source-command emitters and publication\nchecks. `native_scratch.rs` owns identity-bound scratch cleanup. The route adds\nno interpreter argv/file provider or manifest capability.\nThe standalone binary supplies no private-host hooks.\nThe private `source_live_cli` host supplies the versioned durable source CLI,\nheld-directory checkpoint store and restart-stable clock. It derives bindings\nfrom retained Projects and explicit task/read snapshots, then uses the existing\nsource journal and migration driver. A predecessor-held claim restricts CLI\nmigration to one destination; neither journal hashes nor that claim authenticate\na store replaced or rolled back by its owner.\n`crates/semaprax-toolchain` owns the `doctor` implementation and the held-parent\nstaged publication behind its `new`; the compiler library owns the bounded\nstandalone `new` route (`src/project/create.rs`), and both share one grammar and\none scaffold. The toolchain also owns the\nProject Native Rust package publication adapter, and safe Windows revision-store\nhost. Its `rich_native_host` module wraps admitted rich-Cargo builds and native\ncallback dispatch with path-free human/JSON refusals. The private\n`native-authority-check` command inspects selected plan, crate, and tool bytes,\ntarget, trust policy, and per-call effects without launching Cargo or native\ncode; the full CLI does not yet route rich-Cargo builds. Its `opencode_host`\nmodule owns the explicit fixed-provider process,\ntransport receipt binding. `bounded_capture` owns shared Unix nonblocking\nprocess-group capture; `claude_host` owns the separate native Claude print-JSON\ntransport and reported-usage validation for [repair V3](CLAUDE-PRINT-REPAIR-V1.md).\nThe private repair host keeps config parsing and receipt rendering in\n`source_live_cli/repair/config.rs` and `receipt.rs`; both transports retain the\nsame compiler-owned lifecycle, proposal decoder and checkpoint recovery. Its source adapter\nimplements the existing lifecycle `ProposalSource`; compiler-owned `run_live`\nretains canonical proposal admission and checked deterministic stages. The\ncore exposes only the existing read-only retained-value encoding for context.\n`live_invocation/priced` wraps the generic kernel with paired work and money\nreservations. `live_invocation/persistence/priced` commits both in one additive\ncheckpoint envelope; recovery preserves unknown charges and never authorizes\nredispatch. `live_invocation/io` and `persistence/priced_io` own the opt-in v2\nouter envelope's exact logical request bytes, maximum response reservations,\nand successor I/O carry. Monetary and I/O handoffs share one predecessor\nidentity, generation, and chain. Existing generic journal bytes remain unchanged.\nThe source-specific checkpoint grammar lives under\n`src/live_invocation/source_journal`; it uses the existing caller-owned\n`CheckpointStore` and keeps the generic journal wire unchanged. Its validated\nrecovery data supplies the existing cumulative ledger's source restoration\nroute. The v2 execution profile additionally owns full stage-fuel reservations,\ncharged replay reservations, optional usage observations, and terminal snapshots.\n`source_journal/io_v5` owns additive cumulative request/response reservations\nand their nonrefundable migration carry; [Source Live I/O v5](SOURCE-LIVE-IO-V5.md)\ndefines the bound limits and the private CLI v3 projection.\n`source_journal/wait_v7` owns the opt-in combined model-wait inventory, canonical\nwire, replay closure grammar, fuel and phase-specific capacity; `sink` retains\nthe one caller-owned checkpoint writer. Frozen v1-v6 profiles remain separate.\n`source_journal/owned_wait_v8` owns the separate private typed owned-wait\ninventory, exact E/B bindings, phase capacity and fixed same-file append\nadapter. Its `inventory/accounting` child retains the exact Context borrow in\nan incremental authenticated accounting prefix; the target protocol's\n`owned_wait_v8/settlement/accounting` child owns shared reservation/result-charge\nverification. Pure entry checking publishes no authenticated history. Its shared journal container retains the exclusive physical lease;\nborrowers keep that container through owned stages. Physical uncertainty\npermanently poisons the container; pure prospective row refusal does not.\n`live_upstream` owns fresh initialization through real reservation and State\nACKs, followed by one actual Observe and TurnObserved ACK, in an explicitly\nselected initialized profile. Its private `runtime` child owns lifecycle custody independently of disposable\nborrowed session handles and dispatches the existing acknowledged failed-Observe\ncleanup/Stop tail. Its `continue_run` child consumes the retained first Model\nthrough the original Authorize/effect/Reduce/Step ACK joins into the existing\nsecond-turn driver. Success retains only the consumed Report projection; each\nincomplete join retains its physical owner in runtime quarantine. An actual\nfirst-turn failed target retains its typed State owner in runtime custody and\ncan enter the existing acknowledged State cleanup, receipt, and sticky Stop\ndriver; a failed cleanup boundary retains the reached owner without retry.\nThe `failed_state/continued` child retains the actual second-turn failed-target\nState through the same fixed State cleanup/receipt/Stop adapter. Its distinct\ncontinued lineage borrows the original funding hold and checked proposal; it\ncannot reconstruct owners from journal evidence. Normal close is admitted after\nauthenticated Complete Report consumption or acknowledged failure Stop. Pending\nphysical phases refuse normal runtime close; forced host teardown retires\njournal authority before backing release and does not claim semantic settlement.\nThe `runtime/abandonment` child owns the bounded actual Refused route: its\nprivate ACK-created permit allows `registered_stage/authorize/abandonment` to\nconsume the original scalar-only Refused Decision and State. The candidate and\ninventory `refusal` children validate exact inert refusal coordinates, canonical\nState operations and successful receipt before Stop; they cannot create owners.\nThe `runtime/recovered_authorize` child owns exact first-TransferCompleted\nrecovery. `candidate/authorization_recovery` derives inert current-tail facts;\n`live_upstream/authorize` issues a consuming reconstruction permit, and\n`registered_stage/live_run/authorize/recovery` retains materialized State even\nwhen a subsequent guard fails. The physical `store/source_v8/recovery_grant`\nchild binds the one recovered append transition to exact prefix pins. Recovery\nthen reuses charged source Authorize and the existing two-turn owner chain.\nThe `runtime/shutdown` child owns eligible first-model Completed State\nabandonment: its private Started-ACK permit enables the interpreter\n`registered_stage/live_run/shutdown` child to release the original State.\nCandidate/inventory `shutdown` children validate exact Completed basis, wait,\nproposal, compiler operations and observed receipt before Cancelled Stop.\n`runtime/public/shutdown` exposes the opaque prepare/finish/shutdown boundary;\nother quarantined phases retain custody. Public construction is owned by\nthe `runtime/public` child described below.\nIts `wait` child retains the actual helper park;\n`append/checkpoint` seals the frozen v2 frame from the same held session and\nactual witness inventory without exposing the key or restoring an owner. Historical rows cannot\nmint physical owners or permits. The `append/owned_effect/consumed/reduce_hold/terminal`\nchild owns final registry retirement: only consumption of the actual claimed\nComplete Report can settle its same inherited hold against the exact current\nterminal ACK. All incomplete holds retain quarantine on Drop. `append/owned_effect/intent` owns the actual\nheld Intent durable ACK and sealed successor; its callback-free registry\ntransition retains the same exclusive future-Reduce hold. The consuming\n`live_upstream/effect/authorization/prepared/intent/activation` adapter owns\nfresh post-ACK checks and the zero-target-call engine activation permit. Its\n`intent/dispatch` sibling consumes that actual Activated owner and carries the\nprivate invocation accounting ledger with the same hold through one host call;\n`registered_stage/effect/live_append/intent/dispatch` owns the shared legacy\nand live dispatch body.\n`registered_stage/reduce/live_stage` borrows inert full-Step or failure facts\nfrom the actual physical reducer stage, including canonical cleanup vectors\nand observed evaluator fuel; descriptive facts grant no execution or cleanup\nauthority.\nThe source, append, and engine `settlement/cleanup` children retain actual\nRecorded ownership through fixed cleanup ACKs, physical Decision release,\nreceipt settlement, and guarded one-use Outcome handoff with the same ledger\nand future-Reduce hold. Failed target or observer settlement retains its actual\nState obligation; postmint guard loss retains actual Executed ownership.\nThe `observe/settlement/failed_state` and closed continued descendant retain\nactual failed Observe ownership through fixed State-cleanup ACKs. Engine\n`observe/failed_cleanup` captures real per-action outcomes around the existing\nrelease primitive; postrelease checks use actual released holders and cached\nfacts. Append, candidate and fold `failed_observe` children bind the exact\nfailure/vector/Started index and current lineage. Continued cleanup retains the\nsame ledger and Reduce hold; initial cleanup creates neither. These private\nroutes require owning runtime verification before acceptance.\nThe source and append `settlement/cleanup/reduce` children consume that actual\nExecuted owner through the original full-F reservation ACK, spending the same\nprospective hold under the append marker. `registered_stage/reduce/live_stage`\nthen enters the existing evaluator with those same roots and retains Staged\nownership, observed fuel, accounting, and the fresh charged Reduce lineage.\nDefault ObserveOnly remains separate.\nThe later `continue/later/settlement/start/resume` child moves the actual Parked\nowner through the existing continued Resume interpreter with a closed lineage\npermit. Its `observe/settlement/later_carry` Completed selector accepts only the\nsuccessful physical Resumed State, retaining failures and exact observed fuel.\nThe fixed Model writer owns the Completed ACK and cumulative hold transition.\nIts `completed/join` child checks the exact physical Resume/Completed pair and\nmoves the owner into the existing continued authorization/effect/Reduce/Step\npipeline. The source `model/join` child retains the actual request and ACK\nhistory; `continue/join` selects the physical hold from either the first Step\nor the retained later Step. No journal fact constructs this lineage.\nThe append `step/continue/run` child composes the actual first Continue owner\nthrough the second turn and terminal Report projection. It derives the journal\nfrom that physical owner, delegates every ACK and effect to the existing fixed\njoins, and seals each incomplete owner in a private opaque quarantine while\nretiring the store. It is not a public session or a runtime quarantine registry.\n[Source Agent owned wait v1](SOURCE-AGENT-OWNED-WAIT-V1.md) owns these bounded\nprivate successors. Its restart child may reauthenticate only a first-turn\nPrepared prefix, materialize fresh Bytes backing, and consume that owner once\nthrough the original model path under a separate trusted-host grant; later,\nuncertain and post-intent prefixes remain closed. Public Agent execution and\nthe remaining recovery classifications remain unfinished.\nThe `live_upstream/runtime/restart` child consumes that exact Prepared owner\ndirectly into the existing runtime slot before Model continuation. Completed\nModel owners enter the same full two-turn chain as fresh runs; continuation\nfailures retain their reached physical owner in a distinct restart quarantine.\nNo caller session receives a restored owner, new reservation ledger, or store\nauthority. The source-added process and append-fault gates remain unexecuted.\n`source_journal/policy_v6` owns independently folded quote reservations, observed\nand unknown exposure, and cumulative policy carry. Its V6 profile composes I/O\nlimits and restores reservations before source continuation.\n`provider_adapter_sdk/source_bridge/policy` owns ordinary adapter quote admission\nand observed overage accounting; the journal remains the durable authority.\n`provider_adapter_sdk/bridge` implements the generic `ModelHandler` seam over\nexplicit adapter capabilities. It streams deltas through the existing compiled\nProposal decoder before the kernel's independent compiled-schema decode and\nauthorization. `model_budget_policy/live_hook` composes explicit request-bound\nhost token/cost estimates with the existing work hook, retaining conservative\ncharges in memory without claiming generic-journal crash recovery.\n`model_budget_policy/retry` owns bounded in-process adapter attempt scheduling\nand the reservation trail. It consumes an explicit provider factory and host\nbackoff/classification seams; it adds no durable journal or deployment authority.\n`model_budget_policy/durable` derives retained execution and deployment limits.\n`model_routing/engine` is the one deterministic model-routing decision core\n(screen, rules, policy, frozen plans, advisory validation, v2 rendering,\ncache/replay), also mounted as the `publish = false` workspace crate\n`semaprax-decision-core` that `semaprax-harness` re-exports; it has no I/O and\nmints no deployment, grant or transport. `model_routing` is its runtime-facing\nboundary: an untrusted recommendation over host-admitted ids that existing\ndeployment and durable-policy authority rechecks\n([decision core](DECISION-CORE-V1.md)).\n`live_invocation/policy_kernel` and `policy_kernel_v3` compose that scheduler\nwith caller-owned checkpoints; the V3 journal binds exact SDK envelope-byte\nreservations beside frozen V2 policy bytes. Journal recovery validates all\nretained associations before the scheduler can construct an adapter.\n`provider_adapter_sdk/vendor` owns Responses and Messages wire normalization\nbehind the explicit `HostHttpStreamTransport` seam. The host retains origin,\nTLS, proxy and credential configuration; compiler-derived Proposal admission\nremains in the streaming/schema owners.\n`provider_adapter_sdk/vendor/http` implements the native HTTPS seam with\nexplicit origin, TLS and credential configuration, disabled redirects/proxies,\nand bounded buffered responses. It does not provide incremental network polling.\n`authentication` owns explicit Rust-host secrets, bounded Argon2id password\nhashing, authenticated session transitions and account/session composition.\nStorage, entropy, clock and signing authority remain supplied by the embedding\nhost; no source operation or generated backend authority is added. See\n[Authentication host v1](AUTHENTICATION-HOST-V1.md).\n`job_runtime` owns single-job checkpoint persistence and host-driven execution;\n`job_fixture` owns lifecycle decisions and `job_evidence` owns replay validation.\nPayload admission uses a supplied compiled schema; handler implementation and\ncheckpoint storage authority remain explicit host responsibilities.\n`job_runtime/source_handler` binds a retained, effect-free source callable to\na domain-separated deployment identity stored in the existing job descriptor.\nIts checked drive verifies descriptor and schema before the existing runtime\nclaims work; evaluation uses the retained-call interpreter without adding host\nauthority. Imported callable closures remain outside this bounded source route.\n`provider_adapter_sdk/source_bridge` adapts the ordinary source `ProposalSource`\nwith explicit fresh adapter factories, bounded canonical retained context, and\n`streaming_proposal_decode/source` admission against the authoritative source\nProposal schema. `streaming_proposal_decode/grammar` consumes a bounded\nDAG lowered by both schema owners, enforcing nested identity/order/scalar\nrules while retaining final whole-decoder admission. Sorted auxiliary case\nlookups narrow candidates per byte without changing declaration order.\n`AgentRuntimeV2::run_live` consumes that ordinary source\nthrough Direct Runtime v2 only after canonical proposal admission and at the\ntyp